      "side": 1,
      "message": "What is this block trying to do? The `initialized` boolean returned by `EndAccess` is to let the user of Dawn know if the next user of the texture should zero-init it. It seems that in this CL we are tracking the initialized state twice: internally in the WebGPU backend, and in the inner device itself. Both should match because it\u0027s all Dawn frontend that does the logic. Maybe we could have an ASSERT here instead that the two states (the inner texture\u0027s initialized state, and our tracking of the initialized state) match?",
